<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lok Sabha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1952</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as House of the People</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lok <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabha-libya">Sabha</a>, or House of the People, is the lower house of the Parliament of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, first constituted in 1952 after the country's first general election. Its members are elected by universal adult suffrage from single-member constituencies, and the prime minister and council of ministers are responsible to it, making it the dominant chamber of Indian government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lok-sabha.jpg" alt="Lok Sabha" width="320" height="165" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:FlyJet777 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:India_18th_Lok_Sabha_Partywise_2026.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
